// the Opens and the Play-Ins and 3 in the Heats and the Final, and Epic's own
// payload for cup 4 measures out to exactly that. It is what lets the
// elimination half of a score be split back out of the total.
const R_KILL={open:2, playin:2, heat1:3, heat2:3, heat3:3, heat4:3, final:3};

// The experience tally is one pool ranked across every card the game holds, so
// folding a second circuit into it would move the Experience attribute of every
// FNCS card ever built — a silent re-rating of the whole game as the price of
// adding a mode. So EWC stages are ranked against themselves like any other
// stage, but they do not register: a player who also plays FNCS keeps the
// experience their FNCS record earned, and one who does not sits at the middle
// of the distribution.
function mkSortsNoExp(arr){
  return {aim:sortBy(arr,r=>r.avgElims), sur:sortBy(arr,r=>r.survival),
          clu:sortBy(arr,r=>r.wpm),      con:sortBy(arr,r=>r.tpm),
          end:sortBy(arr,r=>r.endShare)};
}

